00:32:41,830 --> 00:32:43,750
and it also need to call some functions to cancel the order.

461
00:32:43,760 --> 00:32:49,430
So in deboss you basically express them in code as error like.

462
00:32:49,430 --> 00:32:51,909
if you see this error call those sequence of functions.

463
00:32:51,919 --> 00:32:57,750
If you see other types of error do something else.

464
00:32:57,750 --> 00:33:02,630
So we do ask users to explicitly specify the roll back actions.

465
00:33:02,630 --> 00:33:04,549
And the roll back actions are also steps.

466
00:33:04,549 --> 00:33:06,549
So the benefit of using deboss is.

467
00:33:06,549 --> 00:33:11,509
that we'll guarantee everything the workflow that all the steps will run to completion.

468
00:33:11,509 --> 00:33:20,231
How do I as a developer take an existing body of code and the annotations that debus wants? What process would I go through?

469
00:33:20,240 --> 00:33:23,190
Yeah, so we think it's pretty easy.

470
00:33:23,190 --> 00:33:25,590
So you first install the library.

471
00:33:25,590 --> 00:33:28,149
Uh if you use Python, it's pip install.

472
00:33:28,149 --> 00:33:30,630
If you use hyperscript, it's npm install.

473
00:33:30,630 --> 00:33:34,070
And then after that, you can just import deboss.

474
00:33:34,080 --> 00:33:38,950
And then you say you have a function you want to be a workflow.

475
00:33:38,950 --> 00:33:41,750
You just decorate it as at deboss.workflow.

476
00:33:41,760 --> 00:33:48,070
and then within that workflow function you will see what function calls it makes.

477
00:33:48,070 --> 00:33:50,389
and then you decorate those functions as at deboss.step.

478
00:33:50,399 --> 00:33:55,269
I think my question was more like how do I figure out.

479
00:33:55,269 --> 00:33:56,870
which functions I should now go and decorate.

480
00:33:56,880 --> 00:33:59,350
All right.

481
00:33:59,350 --> 00:34:01,830
So I think you essentially decorate any functions.

482
00:34:01,830 --> 00:34:04,070
that will talk to external APIs or talk to the database.

483
00:34:04,080 --> 00:34:08,069
anything that will generate side effects outside of your program.

484
00:34:08,079 --> 00:34:10,790
Thanks, Chan.

