00:39:50,390 --> 00:39:56,150
So that it will guarantee basically if I refunded it before I will only refund it once.

564
00:39:56,150 --> 00:40:02,069
So this guarantees that if the user ask I want to refund it again based on the recorded.

565
00:40:02,069 --> 00:40:05,830
information we'll say you've already been refunded before so we'll skip. the refund.

566
00:40:05,830 --> 00:40:10,069
and they will guarantee that once we kick off the refund workflow it will always finish.

567
00:40:10,069 --> 00:40:11,910
So say if something happened to the program.

568
00:40:11,910 --> 00:40:19,990
if it crashes in the middle we will just resume the refund process from where it left off.

569
00:40:19,990 --> 00:40:21,990
So like say if I already process the payment.

570
00:40:21,990 --> 00:40:26,470
or kind of return the money back to user will also restore the inventory and stuff like that.

571
00:40:26,480 --> 00:40:28,870
Basic question though.

572
00:40:28,870 --> 00:40:31,349
So if the agent is the LLM with tool.

573
00:40:31,349 --> 00:40:33,829
and the LLM is the one calling the tool.

574
00:40:33,829 --> 00:40:37,589
which in many cases the tool is an API call.

575
00:40:37,589 --> 00:40:42,790
How does now deboss get involved in that part of the workflow?

576
00:40:42,800 --> 00:40:45,910
Yeah, exactly.

577
00:40:45,910 --> 00:40:50,630
So the cool thing is that as I introduced before deboss is a library.

578
00:40:50,630 --> 00:40:53,670
and annotations that you can wrap around your function with.

579
00:40:53,670 --> 00:40:57,910
So when lm calls the function it will call the wrapped function.

580
00:40:57,910 --> 00:40:59,910
and that wrap function is a dual workflow.

581
00:40:59,910 --> 00:41:06,790
So that's why it's super easy to add deboss with any AI frameworks.

582
00:41:06,790 --> 00:41:12,390
Like instead of passing your bare function, you pass the annotated function into your AI tools.

583
00:41:12,390 --> 00:41:14,390
That's interesting.

584
00:41:14,390 --> 00:41:17,829
Are you going to talk about data pipelines as well? Is there an example there?

